    sampleAnswer: `I walk it in the order it will be brought up, because that is the order faults appear. Power: every rail, regulator type and headroom, decoupling at each supply pin, sequencing. Reset, clock with the load-capacitor arithmetic, boot and configuration straps tied to a defined level, debug and console pinned out. Then every boundary where two parts meet: logic levels against VIH and VOH, 5 volt tolerance from the pin table, pull-ups once at a computed value, termination, protection on anything leaving the box, TX to RX. Then what is missing: test points, a current jumper, net names matching the firmware. I compare with the vendor reference design and ask for a reason behind every difference. Each finding gets an ID, a severity, the net, the datasheet page, the consequence and a proposed change, in a table the designer answers. The faults that cost spins are a floating BOOT0, missing I2C pull-ups and a 5 volt signal into a non-tolerant pin.`,
