    sampleAnswer: `Statement coverage means every statement ran: Level C. Decision coverage adds that every decision was both true and false: Level B. MC/DC, at Level A, adds that every condition is shown to independently change the outcome, meaning for each condition there is a pair of tests that differ only in that condition and give different results. For A and B or C: A's pair is false-true-false with true-true-false, B's is true-false-false with true-true-false, C's is true-false-false with true-false-true. The union is four tests, n plus one, not eight. Two tests, all true and all false, give decision coverage but isolate no condition. When a line is uncovered I analyse it: either a requirement is untested, so I write the test; or the code has no requirement, so I write a derived requirement or remove the code; or it is dead, so I remove or justify it; or it is deactivated, so I show it stays off. I do not write a test only to colour the line.`,
